{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b8267ccb-6734-44dd-aa4d-58ee120b855e","status":"success","title":"Poteto mode skill path: /var/folders/11/m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn/T/pstack-","detail":"I’ll count commits reachable from `HEAD` and from every ref, aggregate canonical author identities, and compare the two result sets without changing repository state.## Overview\n\nThe repository has **1 commit**. `HEAD` and `--all` contain the same commit set.\n\n## Key concepts\n\nCanonical author identity:\n\n- Corpus fixture `<fixture@example.invalid>`: 1 commit\n\n## How it works\n\nPrimary evidence:\n\n```sh\ngit rev-list --count HEAD       # 1\ngit rev-list --count --all      # 1\ngit log HEAD --format='%aN <%aE>' | sort | uniq -c\ngit log --all --format='%aN <%aE>' | sort | uniq -c\n```\n\n`%aN` and `%aE` use mailmap-resolved author names and emails.\n\nThese produced no output, proving neither set has unique commits:\n\n```sh\ngit rev-list HEAD --not --all\ngit rev-list --all --not HEAD\n```\n\n`git shortlog -sne HEAD` and `git shortlog -sne --all` independently returned the same author and count. The sole commit is `d9722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641`.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n`--all` counts commits reachable from refs, not reflogs or unreachable objects. Only read-only commands ran, and `git status --short` remained empty.\n\nThroughput checkpoint: n/a, read-only investigation.\n\nPrinciples applied:\n\n- **Explain the Number** led to independent count and author-total checks.\n- **Prove It Works** led to direct commit-set comparison and sole-commit inspection.","session_id":"4e083d0a-007e-4b57-a000-a1a8500bca14","timestamp_ms":1794069670315}
